# Git commits

- Only commit when the user asks.
- Only push when the user asks. Never force-push.
- Read `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` before committing.
- Match existing commit style: past tense, one sentence, explain why.
- Split unrelated changes into separate commits. Never `git add .`.
- Skip whitespace-only files and leftover `console.log`s unless asked.

```bash
# BAD — stage everything, one mixed commit
git add .
git commit -m "Update stuff"

# GOOD — stage related files, one commit per concern
git add app/wallet/page.tsx components/Wallet/WalletClientContainer.tsx
git commit -m "Fixed wallet layout so balances stay visible on mobile."
```
